    "name": "localFirstCechHilbertDescentAndBranchMultiplicityTheorem",
    "statement": "For a finite connected cover with unitary transition maps, the space of global compatible Hilbert states is the kernel of the Cech equalizer and is canonically the intersection of cycle-holonomy fixed spaces in one root fiber. Its dimension is at most the local fiber dimension, not the product of local dimensions. Compatible coherent projectors descend by intersection with the same fixed space. A central projective cocycle can annihilate ordinary vector sections while retaining projective rays and ordinary endomorphism/descent data. Consequently global Hilbert structure does not by itself imply many actual worlds; nonlinear actualization remains a separate MTT source theorem."
